     bgpd(8) supports the efficient lookup of data within named _s_e_t_s.  An
     aass--sseett, a pprreeffiixx--sseett, and an oorriiggiinn--sseett store AS numbers, prefixes, and
     prefixes/source-as pairs, respectively.  Such sets may be referenced by
     filter rules; see the _F_I_L_T_E_R section for details.  It is more efficient
     to evaluate a set than a long series of rules for filtering each of its
     members.

     One single rrooaa--sseett may be defined, against which bgpd(8) will validate
     the origin of each prefix.  The rrooaa--sseett and the aassppaa--sseett are merged with
     the corresponding tables received via rrttrr sessions.

     A set definition can span multiple lines, and an optional comma is al‐
     lowed between elements.  The same set can be defined more than once, in
     this case the definitions are merged into one common set.

     aass--sseett _n_a_m_e {{ _a_s_-_n_u_m_b_e_r _._._. }}
             An aass--sseett stores AS numbers, and can be used with the AS specific
             parameter in _F_I_L_T_E_R rules.

     aassppaa--sseett {{ ccuussttoommeerr--aass _a_s_-_n_u_m_b_e_r [eexxppiirreess _s_e_c_o_n_d_s] pprroovviiddeerr--aass {{
             _a_s_-_n_u_m_b_e_r ...... }} ...... }}
             The aassppaa--sseett holds a collection of _V_a_l_i_d_a_t_e_d _A_S_P_A _P_a_y_l_o_a_d_s
             (VAPs).  Each as AS_PATH received from an eBGP peer is checked
             against the aassppaa--sseett, and the ASPA Validation State (AVS) is set.
             eexxppiirreess can be set to the seconds since Epoch until when this VAP
             is valid.

                   aspa-set {
                           customer-as 64511 provider-as { 64496 65496 }
                           customer-as 64496 provider-as { 65496 64544 }
                   }

     oorriiggiinn--sseett _n_a_m_e {{ _a_d_d_r_e_s_s/_l_e_n [mmaaxxlleenn _m_l_e_n] ssoouurrccee--aass _a_s_n _._._. }}
             An oorriiggiinn--sseett stores prefix/source-as pairs, and can be used to
             filter on the combination by using the oorriiggiinn--sseett parameter in
             _F_I_L_T_E_R rules.

                   origin-set private { 10.0.0.0/8 maxlen 24 source-as 64511
                                        203.0.113.0/24 source-as 64496 }

     pprreeffiixx--sseett _n_a_m_e {{ _a_d_d_r_e_s_s/_l_e_n _._._. }}
             A pprreeffiixx--sseett stores network prefixes and can be used in place of
             the pprreeffiixx parameter in _F_I_L_T_E_R rules, and in nneettwwoorrkk statements.
             A prefix can be followed by the prefixlen operators listed for
