     _N_E_I_G_H_B_O_R_S _A_N_D _G_R_O_U_P_S section.  The description is used when logging but
     has no further meaning to bgpd(8).

     The mpe(4) interface will be used as the outgoing interface for routes to
     the VPN, and local networks will be announced with the MPLS label speci‐
     fied on the interface.  The interface can provide VPN connectivity for
     another rdomain by being configured in that rdomain.  The required rdo‐
     main must be configured on the interface before bgpd(8) uses it.  Multi‐
     ple VPNs may be connected to a single rdomain, including the rdomain that
     bgpd(8) is running in.

     An example hostname.if(5) configuration for an mpe(4) interface providing
     connectivity to rdomain 1:

           rdomain 1
           mplslabel 2000
           inet 192.198.0.1 255.255.255.255
           up

